Bug 548507 - Retain related attachments without Content-ID when composing. r=maxe, mkmelin

Related parts without Content-ID or Content-Location are visible in the
reader, but their initial parse_begin call suppresses output in compose
mode and marks them as hidden. Attachment replay then skips them during
Forward and Edit as New.

Defer their parsing in compose mode to the existing attachment replay at
EOF, preserving their visibility and encoded content.

Extend the xpcshell inline-forward regression to parts without either
location header, with and without an explicit attachment disposition.
Compare the decoded outgoing names, exact sizes, and every attachment
byte with memory and temporary-file buffering and padded base64.

Keep a small browser test for reader attachment visibility and matching
attachment counts and filenames in Edit as New.

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330751

diff --git a/mailnews/mime/src/mimemrel.cpp b/mailnews/mime/src/mimemrel.cpp
--- a/mailnews/mime/src/mimemrel.cpp
+++ b/mailnews/mime/src/mimemrel.cpp
@@ -435,12 +435,13 @@ static bool MimeMultipartRelated_output_
       }
     }
 
     if (!location) {
-      // Without Content-ID or Content-Location this part is unreachable via
-      // cid: rewriting. Output it as a normal attachment so data is not
-      // silently discarded.
-      return true;
+      // Without Content-ID or Content-Location this part cannot be referenced.
+      // Keep it visible as a normal attachment. When composing, defer parsing
+      // to the attachment replay at EOF; parse_begin would otherwise suppress
+      // output and mark the part as hidden.
+      return !(obj->options && obj->options->decompose_file_p);
     }
 
     char* base_url =
         MimeHeaders_get(child->headers, HEADER_CONTENT_BASE, false, false);
